WEBVTT

00:06.007 --> 00:08.073
[music playing]

00:22.289 --> 00:24.123
- [Lawrence III]
 Disturb not the harmony

00:24.125 --> 00:27.126
 of Fire, Ice, or Lightning,

00:27.128 --> 00:29.528
 lest these Titans
 wreak destruction

00:29.530 --> 00:32.297
 upon the world
 in which they clash.

00:33.667 --> 00:36.101
 Though the water's
 great Guardian

00:36.103 --> 00:38.570
 shall arise
 to quell the fighting,

00:38.572 --> 00:41.040
 alone its song will fail,

00:41.042 --> 00:44.243
 thus the Earth
 shall turn to ash.

00:44.245 --> 00:47.780
O, Chosen One,

00:47.782 --> 00:51.650
into thine hands
bring together all three.

00:51.652 --> 00:54.653
Their treasures combined,

00:54.655 --> 00:58.223
tame the Beast of the Sea.

01:00.194 --> 01:03.228
Now it begins.

01:03.230 --> 01:05.197
- [alarm blares]
- Hmm?

01:05.199 --> 01:07.533
- [computer] Analysis indicates
 that the Titan of Fire

01:07.535 --> 01:10.202
 referred to
 in the ancient inscription

01:10.204 --> 01:12.337
 is the legendary
 Pok�mon Moltres,

01:12.339 --> 01:14.073
 believed to have originated

01:14.075 --> 01:16.842
  in a remote region
  of the Orange Islands.

01:16.844 --> 01:20.112
 The Titan of Lightning
 is the Pok�mon Zapdos,

01:20.114 --> 01:22.748
 and Articuno
 is the Titan of Ice.

01:22.750 --> 01:25.517
 Historical documents confirm

01:25.519 --> 01:28.854
 that the three legendary
 Pok�mon are unique species

01:28.856 --> 01:32.524
 found only in the vicinity
 of Shamouti Island.

01:34.662 --> 01:37.729
- Moltres, Zapdos, and Articuno.

01:38.732 --> 01:40.365
Any one of them would be

01:40.367 --> 01:43.168
a priceless addition
to my collection,

01:43.170 --> 01:45.871
but together,
they are the three keys

01:45.873 --> 01:49.341
that unlock
the ultimate treasure.

01:49.343 --> 01:51.677
- [computer] Pok�mon
 matching subject parameters

01:51.679 --> 01:55.481
 Moltres, Articuno,
 Zapdos detected.

01:55.483 --> 01:57.216
- Then let's get started.

02:01.856 --> 02:03.822
Which one is nearest?

02:03.824 --> 02:05.791
- The Fire Pok�mon, Moltres.

02:05.793 --> 02:07.259
- Good.

03:25.573 --> 03:27.539
- [squawks]

03:31.212 --> 03:33.278
[squawks]

03:34.481 --> 03:36.682
- Now the chase is on.

03:39.453 --> 03:41.453
- [squawking]

04:09.650 --> 04:11.683
- Well, I've taken
the first piece

04:11.685 --> 04:13.552
without much difficulty.

04:13.554 --> 04:16.421
It's like
a simple game of chess.

04:16.423 --> 04:20.425
Next I'll capture Zapdos
and Articuno soon after,

04:20.427 --> 04:23.662
and that
will flush out the king.

04:23.664 --> 04:28.600
And then that's when the game
is going to get interesting.

04:28.602 --> 04:31.036
Bring together all three,

04:31.038 --> 04:37.743
their treasures combined tame
the Beast of the Sea, Lugia.

04:37.745 --> 04:39.711
- [Lugia singing]

04:48.455 --> 04:50.455
[music playing]

05:12.746 --> 05:14.746
[waves lapping]

05:22.423 --> 05:24.723
- [narrator] Another perfect day
 in paradise.

05:24.725 --> 05:26.525
 The weather, warm.

05:26.527 --> 05:28.327
 The breezes, balmy.

05:28.329 --> 05:30.762
 The water,
 calm and crystal clear.

05:30.764 --> 05:34.433
 Even Pok�mon trainers deserve
 a break on a day like today,

05:34.435 --> 05:37.069
 and as our heroes sail
 through the Orange Islands,

05:37.071 --> 05:40.005
 Ash Ketchum dreams
 of his next big adventure.

05:40.007 --> 05:43.342
 Little does he know
 it will be his greatest.

05:44.345 --> 05:46.611
- [yawns] Nice day!

05:46.613 --> 05:49.081
- It's beautiful, right, Togepi?

05:49.083 --> 05:50.615
- Togepi!

05:50.617 --> 05:52.117
- Hey, Ash, think we have time

05:52.119 --> 05:54.519
to give the Pok�mon
a little fresh air?

05:54.521 --> 05:56.988
- Sure, Tracey.
It'll take us about an hour

05:56.990 --> 05:58.790
to get to the next island.

05:58.792 --> 06:00.125
There's plenty of time.

06:00.127 --> 06:02.961
- Well, what are we waiting for?

