of the Orange Islands.

09:29.937 --> 09:31.937
- [Magikarp chattering]

09:44.251 --> 09:46.251
- [groaning]

09:48.155 --> 09:49.588
- An island!

09:49.590 --> 09:50.622
- In a storm!

09:50.624 --> 09:52.290
- I've seen this movie.

09:52.292 --> 09:56.161
- Oh? Do we have karp insurance?

09:56.163 --> 09:57.162
- Huh?

09:57.164 --> 09:58.797
- We're about to be...

09:58.799 --> 10:00.231
- Filet of fish.

10:00.233 --> 10:01.366
- [Magikarp chattering]

10:01.368 --> 10:03.134
- [Team Rocket yell]

10:08.208 --> 10:10.208
- [cooing]

10:22.089 --> 10:24.255
- Mime, Mime, Mime, Mime.

10:24.257 --> 10:25.724
Mime, Mime, Mime, Mime...

10:25.726 --> 10:27.025
- Good morning, Delia.

10:27.027 --> 10:29.294
Well, you certainly
do have a green thumb.

10:29.296 --> 10:31.730
- Oh, thanks, Professor,
but the truth is

10:31.732 --> 10:34.065
I've been getting a lot of help
with my garden lately.

10:34.067 --> 10:36.101
The weather's been
just beautiful.

10:36.103 --> 10:39.237
- Well, this is the time of year
when the sun shines every day.

10:39.239 --> 10:41.072
[chuckles] Mm.

10:41.074 --> 10:42.340
- Mime?

10:47.114 --> 10:49.414
Mime. Mime, Mime, Mime!

10:52.753 --> 10:54.853
- Oh. [grumbling]

10:59.693 --> 11:02.394
Say, that was awfully strange.

11:02.396 --> 11:05.263
- And it passed by so quickly.

11:05.265 --> 11:07.399
Oh, my! It looks like snow!

11:07.401 --> 11:08.366
- Huh?
- Huh?

11:09.369 --> 11:11.770
- [Delia] It is snow,

11:11.772 --> 11:13.972
but this is summer.

11:13.974 --> 11:16.141
How can it snow?

11:16.143 --> 11:18.176
- I--I don't know.

11:18.178 --> 11:19.344
- Mime!

11:19.346 --> 11:20.045
- [both] Hmm? [gasps]

11:24.117 --> 11:26.117
- [cooing]

11:41.334 --> 11:42.333
- [Delia gasps]

11:44.104 --> 11:45.937
- Mime, Mime.
- [both] Huh?

11:45.939 --> 11:47.906
- [Diglett chattering]

11:50.243 --> 11:52.243
- Huh? [gasping]

11:54.948 --> 11:56.781
- Mime, Mime, Mime,
Mime, Mime, Mime...

11:56.783 --> 11:58.116
- What is it, Mimey?

11:58.118 --> 11:59.784
- Mime, Mime, Mime, Mime!

11:59.786 --> 12:01.753
- Mr. Mime is very upset.

12:01.755 --> 12:04.856
- Yes, and so are
the other Pok�mon.

12:04.858 --> 12:08.159
Pok�mon are more in tune
with nature than we are.

12:08.161 --> 12:10.762
When something goes wrong,
they can sense it,

12:10.764 --> 12:12.731
and I'm afraid
something somewhere

12:12.733 --> 12:14.432
is going terribly wrong.

12:26.246 --> 12:28.213
- We sure are lucky.

12:28.215 --> 12:30.982
- If we hadn't found this place,
we'd be in real trouble.

12:30.984 --> 12:32.784
- Togepi!
- [Tracey] Ahh!

12:32.786 --> 12:35.253
Uh, I think we still might be.

12:35.255 --> 12:36.254
- Huh?
- Hmm?

12:36.256 --> 12:37.222
[both yell]

12:41.361 --> 12:43.228
- [gasping]
- [shuddering]

12:48.301 --> 12:50.468
- Toge.
- Maren, how are you?

12:50.470 --> 12:51.436
- Toge!
- Huh?

12:53.440 --> 12:55.106
- It's been a while.

12:55.108 --> 12:56.841
- Carol, I can't believe it.

12:56.843 --> 12:58.409
It's great to see you.

12:58.411 --> 13:00.879
- [Carol] What are you doing
back on Shamouti Island?

13:00.881 --> 13:03.214
- [Maren] We got up caught up
in that storm and floated in,

13:03.216 --> 13:05.517
and it looks like we got here
at the perfect time.

13:05.519 --> 13:08.987
- You're right. The annual
Legend Festival starts today.

13:08.989 --> 13:11.022
- This is my favorite
island holiday.

13:11.024 --> 13:13.124
Are you gonna be
the star of the show again?

13:13.126 --> 13:16.094
- No, I'm too old to be
the Festival Maiden anymore,

13:16.096 --> 13:19.197
so this year, my little sister
is gonna take over for me.

13:19.199 --> 13:21.099
- Wonder where she could--
- I'm right here!

13:21.101 --> 13:24.402
The only one not wearing
some stupid costume.

13:24.404 --> 13:26.171
You'd think
after a few centuries,

13:26.173 --> 13:28.206
you'd have outgrown
this dorky ritual.

13:28.208 --> 13:29.841
- It's our tradition!

13:29.843 --> 13:31.976
You should be honored
to take part!

13:31.978 --> 13:34.979
- Don't worry. I'll play
my role in the big legend.

13:34.981 --> 13:37.148
I've only seen you do it,
like, a zillion times.

13:37.150 --> 13:38.850
- Just be there!

13:38.852 --> 13:41.052
Well, unfortunately,
that's my little sister.

13:41.054 --> 13:43.955
Her name is Melody,
but don't get fooled.

13:43.957 --> 13:47.192
She's not always this adorable.
Who's this?

13:47.194 --> 13:49.460
- [Maren] Oh, sorry.
This is Ash Ketchum.

13:49.462 --> 13:50.962
He's a Pok�mon trainer.

13:50.964 --> 13:52.230
- [crowd] Pok�mon trainer?!

13:52.232 --> 13:53.331
- Hmm?

13:53.333 --> 13:56.301
- [cheering]

13:56.303 --> 13:58.870
- [Elder] The ancient legend
foretells your arrival,

13:58.872 --> 14:02.040
and only with you,
can the Guardian of the waters

14:02.042 --> 14:06.511
vanquish the great Titans
of Fire, Ice, and Lightning!

14:06.513 --> 14:10.281
In your hands, O, Chosen One,

14:10.283 --> 14:12.450
in your hands
rests the world and its fate.

14:12.452 --> 14:13.918
- It does?

14:13.920 --> 14:16.254
- Heh. Don't let it
worry you, kid.

14:16.256 --> 14:18.122
It's just for the tourists!

14:18.124 --> 14:19.390
Blasted beak.

14:19.392 --> 14:21.593
- So you're
a Pok�mon trainer, huh?

14:21.595 --> 14:24.295
Hmm, I guess he'll do.

14:24.297 --> 14:27.866
Here's your traditional
welcome kiss.

14:27.868 --> 14:30.101
- Toge toge toge!
- [shudders]

14:31.638 --> 14:33.171
- Are you his little sister?

14:33.173 --> 14:34.639
- I am not!

14:34.641 --> 14:37.508
- Well, then I guess
you must be his girlfriend.

14:37.510 --> 14:40.144
- Ugh, gross!
- Oh, I don't think so.

14:40.146 --> 14:43.314
I'll be glad to play for him
tonight at the Legend Banquet.

14:43.316 --> 14:44.549
Starts around 8:00.

14:44.551 --> 14:46.484
Oh, and Misty,

14:46.486 --> 14:48.553
try not to get jealous.

14:48.555 --> 14:50.455
- [growls]
- [chuckles]

14:50.457 --> 14:53.057
- We have found our Chosen One!

14:53.059 --> 14:55.093
- [cheering]

15:13.146 --> 15:15.980
- [drums playing]
- [singers] Hah!

15:15.982 --> 15:17.649
[music playing]

15:36.503 --> 15:38.937
- Hurry! Hurry!
Deep-fried festival cakes!

15:38.939 --> 15:39.704
Get 'em while they're hot!

15:41.374 --> 15:43.374
[music fades]

15:45.045 --> 15:47.178
[overlapping chatter]

15:47.180 --> 15:50.415
- And she says,
"No, but I have Krabbies."

15:50.417 --> 15:53.284
- [laughter]

15:53.286 --> 15:55.119
- [Elder] Heh. Krabbies.

15:55.121 --> 15:56.421
- That's ridiculous,

15:56.423 --> 15:58.489
me, Ash's girlfriend.

16:00.126 --> 16:02.593
It's totally ridiculous.

16:02.595 --> 16:04.495
- I can't wait
to see what my part

16:04.497 --> 16:06.130
in the Legend Ceremony's
gonna be.

16:06.132 --> 16:08.166
- Hmm? [grumbles]

16:08.168 --> 16:10.201
- [playing music]

16:10.203 --> 16:11.169
- Ah?
- Huh?

16:23.616 --> 16:27.051
- Ash, that's her,
the girl we met on the beach.

16:27.053 --> 16:28.186
- Melody.

16:28.188 --> 16:29.454
- Melody?

16:43.570 --> 16:45.703
- Hmph! She's a big show-off.

16:52.512 --> 16:55.279
[applause]

16:55.281 --> 16:57.348
- Hear ye, all!

16:57.350 --> 17:01.319
From the trio of islands,
ancient spheres shall you take,

17:01.321 --> 17:05.223
for between life and death,
all the difference you'll make.

17:05.225 --> 17:06.524
O, Chosen One,

17:06.526 --> 17:08.393
you must climb to the shrine

17:08.395 --> 17:10.128
to right what is wrong,

17:10.130 --> 17:12.797
and the world will be healed
by the Guardian's song.

17:12.799 --> 17:15.500
- What do I do?
- I just told you, Ash.

17:15.502 --> 17:19.303
- Yeah. I heard all that stuff,
but what do I have to do?

17:19.305 --> 17:22.540
- Oh, it won't be very hard,
Ash, not for you.

17:22.542 --> 17:26.177
And besides, almost all
the Chosen Ones come back alive.

17:26.179 --> 17:27.412
- Melody!

17:27.414 --> 17:29.680
- [giggles] All you have to do

17:29.682 --> 17:32.250
is get these glass balls
from three islands,

17:32.252 --> 17:35.086
one from Fire Island,
one from Ice Island,

17:35.088 --> 17:36.554
and one from Lightning Island,

17:36.556 --> 17:39.390
and you bring 'em
to the shrine back here,

17:39.392 --> 17:43.361
and then I celebrate
by playing this song.

17:43.363 --> 17:47.331
[plays music]

17:47.333 --> 17:49.767
Then it's over, O, Chosen One.

17:49.769 --> 17:52.703
- Do I get to wear
a cool costume?

17:52.705 --> 17:55.506
- Sorry, but it's
just come as you are.

17:57.744 --> 18:00.611
Besides, you look perfect to me,

18:00.613 --> 18:03.381
the handsomest Chosen One
in years.

18:03.383 --> 18:06.117
- Okay! Get me a boat,
and I'm ready!

18:06.119 --> 18:09.120
- Oh, there's no hurry.
You have all day tomorrow.

18:09.122 --> 18:10.855
Tonight's just for the party.

18:10.857 --> 18:12.757
Stay. Have some fun!

18:12.759 --> 18:15.259
- Well, some things
are more important than fun.

18:15.261 --> 18:16.828
I'm Ash, the Chosen One!

18:16.830 --> 18:20.164
This is serious.
I gotta be responsible.

18:20.166 --> 18:21.566
- Toge toge.
- That's a switch.

18:21.568 --> 18:23.367
- [trills]

18:23.369 --> 18:25.169
- [Maren] You know what?
- Hmm?

18:25.171 --> 18:27.805
I like your attitude.
We can take my boat, Ash.

18:27.807 --> 18:30.341
- Then let's go!
You coming, Misty?

18:30.343 --> 18:32.176
- No, thanks.
If you want somebody

18:32.178 --> 18:34.345
to do whatever you want
whenever you want,

18:34.347 --> 18:36.814
you should find yourself
a girlfriend!

18:36.816 --> 18:38.616
- Toge tog.

18:38.618 --> 18:40.852
- [Ash] Pikachu!

18:40.854 --> 18:42.887
Pikachu?!

18:42.889 --> 18:44.422
- Pika!

18:45.458 --> 18:47.425
- Hey, give me back my hat!

18:55.301 --> 18:57.301
- [all moaning]

18:59.272 --> 19:00.838
- Our ship is ruined.

19:00.840 --> 19:02.473
- I'm sick over it.

19:02.475 --> 19:04.542
- I'm seasick over it.

19:04.544 --> 19:05.710
- [all moan]

19:05.712 --> 19:06.878
- Eh?
- Eh?

19:10.216 --> 19:11.749
- [Meowth] Huh?

19:15.488 --> 19:17.255
- [Team Rocket yells]

19:22.328 --> 19:23.494
- Wasn't that...

19:23.496 --> 19:24.495
- The twerp?

19:24.497 --> 19:25.663
- And Pikachu, too.

19:28.701 --> 19:31.435
[thunder crashing]

19:31.437 --> 19:32.770
- Huh?
- Huh?

19:32.772 --> 19:35.273
- [moaning]

19:35.275 --> 19:36.574
[all yell]

19:38.912 --> 19:44.682
- Disturb not the harmony
of Fire, Ice, and Lightning.

19:47.487 --> 19:50.821
Ah, what a mess.

20:06.339 --> 20:09.840
- I hope the Legend Ceremony
doesn't include...

20:09.842 --> 20:11.475
a funeral.

20:15.548 --> 20:17.281
- This storm's bad.

20:17.283 --> 20:19.817
What if those two
can't make it to the island?

20:19.819 --> 20:21.752
Carol, I have to take your boat.

20:21.754 --> 20:23.721
- But, Melody, what can you do?

20:23.723 --> 20:25.223
- They're caught
out in the storm

20:25.225 --> 20:27.225
because of our stupid ritual,

20:27.227 --> 20:29.660
and I'm the one
who picked Ash for it.

20:29.662 --> 20:31.862
I just hope they're all right.

20:37.503 --> 20:39.503
- [all grunting, panting]

20:42.375 --> 20:43.374
- [Meowth] Huh?

20:46.846 --> 20:48.546
- What are you coming for?

20:48.548 --> 20:50.815
- To find Ash!
And before you start saying

20:50.817 --> 20:54.285
it's because I secretly
like him, don't, 'cause I don't!

20:54.287 --> 20:56.454
- Hey, chill out!
You sure are sensitive

20:56.456 --> 20:58.322
about somebody
who's not your boyfriend.

20:58.324 --> 20:59.657
- He's not my boyfriend!

20:59.659 --> 21:01.025
He's a boy, and he's a friend,

21:01.027 --> 21:02.893
but he's not a boyfriend!

21:02.895 --> 21:04.428
- You talking about me?

21:04.430 --> 21:05.663
- Togepi!

21:20.046 --> 21:22.313
- Heh.
- What we won't do...

21:22.315 --> 21:23.581
- For Pikachu.

21:23.583 --> 21:25.316
- Heh heh!

21:34.394 --> 21:36.427
- [Lawrence III]
Disturb not the harmony

21:36.429 --> 21:40.598
of Fire, Ice, and Lightning.
[chuckles]

21:40.600 --> 21:45.703
It seems there's been
a shift in the balance of power.

21:45.705 --> 21:48.639
- Pok�mon Zapdos detected.

21:53.413 --> 21:54.478
- [announcer]
 Experts now believe

21:54.480 --> 21:55.780
 that the weather disasters

21:55.782 --> 21:57.648
 occurring in all parts
 of the globe

21:57.650 --> 22:00.451
 are due to a powerful and
 previously unknown phenomenon

22:00.453 --> 22:03.421
 from deep beneath the surface
 of the ocean.

22:03.423 --> 22:06.524
 This is a simulation
 of the underwater river

22:06.526 --> 22:08.859
 that has snaked its way
 around the planet,

22:08.861 --> 22:10.928
 disrupting ocean currents,
 weather patterns,

22:10.930 --> 22:13.431
 and the entire global climate.

22:13.433 --> 22:17.034
- I wonder if this is what's
been upsetting all the Pok�mon.

22:17.036 --> 22:18.102
- [yelps]
- [gasps]

22:18.104 --> 22:19.070
- The source of the disturbance

22:19.072 --> 22:20.838
 appears to be centered

22:20.840 --> 22:22.673
 at the north central region
 of the Orange Islands.

22:22.675 --> 22:24.475
- The Orange Islands?
- [gasps]

22:24.477 --> 22:27.044
But that's where Ash
and his friends are right now.

22:27.046 --> 22:28.479
- [screen rings]
- Oh.

22:28.481 --> 22:30.114
Someone's calling.

22:30.116 --> 22:31.849
 - ...an imbalance in some
 unknown natural force...

22:31.851 --> 22:33.584
 - Professor,
 we're having problems.

22:33.586 --> 22:35.586
- [Brock yells] 
- What is it, Professor Ivy?

22:35.588 --> 22:38.723
 - The Pok�mon here
 are behaving very strangely.

22:44.864 --> 22:46.430
- It looks like
the storm's over.

22:46.432 --> 22:48.132
- But the sea
keeps getting rougher!

23:02.749 --> 23:05.516
- [Ash gasping]

23:10.089 --> 23:11.389
- [Maren gasps]

23:22.969 --> 23:24.068
Ah! The rudder!

23:24.070 --> 23:26.170
- Pikachu!
- [both yell]

23:28.941 --> 23:30.474
[both yell]

23:34.113 --> 23:35.713
- [yells]
- Pika!

23:37.884 --> 23:38.883
- Pi?
- Huh?

23:50.463 --> 23:52.163
- [Maren] Well,
at least we made it, but...

23:52.165 --> 23:53.764
- Pika!
- Pikachu!

23:53.766 --> 23:54.865
Where you going?

23:54.867 --> 23:56.000
- Ash, we shouldn't split up!

23:56.002 --> 23:57.535
The storm might kick up again!

23:59.005 --> 24:01.439
- Pikachu's been acting
really weird!

24:01.441 --> 24:03.073
I gotta find out why!

24:03.075 --> 24:05.476
- Huh? Hmm.

24:13.619 --> 24:14.985
- Okay, hold on, guys!

24:19.659 --> 24:21.625
- [yelling]

24:24.163 --> 24:25.729
- [Misty] Cool move!

24:25.731 --> 24:26.931
- I've been around boats
all my life.

24:26.933 --> 24:28.499
You don't have to be scared.

24:28.501 --> 24:30.868
- Oh, I never get scared
out in the ocean.

24:30.870 --> 24:33.003
I come from a Water Pok�mon Gym.

24:34.207 --> 24:36.140
- [all gasp]

24:43.983 --> 24:46.083
[yelling]

24:52.058 --> 24:54.124
[yelling fades]

25:15.615 --> 25:16.714
- Whaah!

25:24.223 --> 25:25.623
Huh?

25:25.625 --> 25:28.259
- [Tracey]
Hey, are you guys okay?

25:28.261 --> 25:29.860
- Yeah, we're fine!

25:29.862 --> 25:32.530
But I think the boat's
in pretty bad shape.

25:32.532 --> 25:33.697
- [Melody] Where's Ash?

25:33.699 --> 25:35.299
- Up there!

25:35.301 --> 25:36.267
- Huh?
- Huh?

25:40.172 --> 25:42.273
[all yelling]

25:43.809 --> 25:45.276
- We're... slipping!

25:53.219 --> 25:54.218
- [both yelp]

26:01.928 --> 26:03.727
- It flies?

26:06.866 --> 26:08.198
- If you know how.

26:08.200 --> 26:09.833
- Awesome!
- Hang on!

26:09.835 --> 26:11.035
- [Misty groans]

26:14.674 --> 26:15.873
Let's find Ash,

26:15.875 --> 26:17.708
- Yeah,
and if he needs any help,

26:17.710 --> 26:19.276
his girlfriend's here.

26:19.278 --> 26:21.178
- But I'm not--
- Well, like you said,

26:21.180 --> 26:23.747
you are a girl,
and you are his friend.

26:23.749 --> 26:25.683
Isn't that right?

26:25.685 --> 26:27.351
- [chuckles]

26:27.353 --> 26:28.319
Mm.

26:33.593 --> 26:35.859
- [squawking]

26:35.861 --> 26:39.063
- Poor Moltres.
You seem so miserable.

26:40.299 --> 26:43.334
But they say
misery loves company.

26:46.772 --> 26:49.807
 - Zapdos approaching
 Fire Island.

26:51.744 --> 26:52.743
- Pi.

26:53.980 --> 26:55.279
- Pikachu!

27:02.088 --> 27:04.088
[Ash panting]

27:05.891 --> 27:07.024
- Hey, look.

27:07.026 --> 27:08.125
- There they are.

27:08.127 --> 27:09.793
- I can't believe our luck.

27:09.795 --> 27:11.028
- Yeah.

27:11.030 --> 27:12.896
- Pikachu...
- We'll get you.

27:12.898 --> 27:14.765
- [all laugh]

27:37.923 --> 27:39.223
- Oh.

27:40.693 --> 27:44.261
- Pika. Pika Pika Pikachu.

27:46.065 --> 27:47.164
- [gasps]

27:47.166 --> 27:48.999
The ancient sphere.

27:50.036 --> 27:52.069
[grunting]

27:53.739 --> 27:55.973
- Pikachu! Pika! Pika!

28:11.257 --> 28:12.256
- [gasps]

28:15.394 --> 28:16.393
- Pika.

28:19.965 --> 28:22.132
- [Meowth] Guess who, Pikachu.

28:22.134 --> 28:23.100
- Pika?

28:23.102 --> 28:24.802
- Huh? Was that...

28:24.804 --> 28:28.138
- Prepare for more trouble
than you've ever seen.

28:28.140 --> 28:30.474
- And make it double.
We're on the big screen.

28:30.476 --> 28:32.409
- [Ash] I'll have
to catch this on video.

28:32.411 --> 28:33.744
- [Team Rocket gasps]

28:33.746 --> 28:35.012
- I'm in a hurry here,

28:35.014 --> 28:36.714
and the weather's looking bad!

28:36.716 --> 28:39.416
- It has been bad.
Isn't that always our luck?

28:39.418 --> 28:40.851
But our luck's changed,

28:40.853 --> 28:43.053
and our ship
has finally come in!

28:43.055 --> 28:44.421
- Huh?

28:44.423 --> 28:46.390
- [all yelling]

28:48.327 --> 28:49.393
- [Ash yelps]

28:54.967 --> 28:56.400
- Pi.

28:56.402 --> 28:58.335
- Well, I hope you're happy,
Mr. Hero.

28:58.337 --> 29:00.337
If you'd just listened to me
in the first place

29:00.339 --> 29:02.339
and stayed at the party
like I told you to,

29:02.341 --> 29:04.775
we wouldn't be stranded
out here on this island!

29:04.777 --> 29:06.143
- Welcome to my world.

29:06.145 --> 29:08.245
I have to deal with
this stubborn attitude

29:08.247 --> 29:10.981
- every single day.
- Oh, you'll get used to it.

29:10.983 --> 29:12.883
It's just something
you're gonna need to work on

29:12.885 --> 29:14.752
when the two of you
get married.

29:14.754 --> 29:15.919
- Take that back!

29:15.921 --> 29:17.187
- Listen to me, kid.

29:17.189 --> 29:19.123
When you get involved
with the opposite sex,

29:19.125 --> 29:20.924
you're only asking for trouble.

29:20.926 --> 29:24.194
- Yes, and that's the kind
of trouble I stay out of.

29:24.196 --> 29:26.230
- Youse two don't need
the opposite sex,

29:26.232 --> 29:27.498
'cause you got each other.

29:27.500 --> 29:28.532
- What does that mean?

29:28.534 --> 29:29.500
- [laughs]
- Not funny.

29:34.140 --> 29:36.406
- [Jessie yells]
- [James whimpers]

29:36.408 --> 29:38.375
- Pikachu, it's Zapdos.

29:38.377 --> 29:39.376
- Pika.

29:39.378 --> 29:41.478
- [squawks]

29:55.027 --> 29:57.161
[squawks]

29:57.163 --> 29:59.029
- [all yell]

30:03.969 --> 30:05.202
- [squawks]

30:05.204 --> 30:07.104
- Pi.

30:07.106 --> 30:08.205
- Pikachu, no!

30:08.207 --> 30:09.173
- Pika.

30:12.444 --> 30:13.577
Pika!

30:14.980 --> 30:16.280
- Are you okay?

30:16.282 --> 30:17.881
Huh? [gasps]

30:17.883 --> 30:20.450
- [squawks]

30:24.824 --> 30:27.958
- [all gasping]

30:36.202 --> 30:37.935
- Pi.

30:37.937 --> 30:38.969
Pi.

30:38.971 --> 30:40.404
Pika!

30:40.406 --> 30:42.372
- [squawking]

30:43.442 --> 30:45.075
- Pika!

30:46.278 --> 30:47.544
Pika!

30:47.546 --> 30:49.179
- Pikachu's pretty tough,

30:49.181 --> 30:52.082
but Zapdos isn't even
feeling its attacks.

30:52.084 --> 30:54.084
- Those aren't attacks, Jessie.

30:54.086 --> 30:56.119
Pikachu's trying
to talk to Zapdos.

30:56.121 --> 30:57.621
- Pika!
- It's saying,

30:57.623 --> 31:00.624
"What are you doing over here
on Fire Island, Zapdos,

31:00.626 --> 31:02.326
and where's Moltres?"

31:02.328 --> 31:04.294
- Good questions.

31:04.296 --> 31:06.096
- Pika!

31:12.137 --> 31:13.470
- [squawks]

31:13.472 --> 31:15.339
- [gasps]

31:15.341 --> 31:17.007
- Pi.
- Huh?

31:17.009 --> 31:19.910
- [squawking]

31:19.912 --> 31:21.445
- Translation?
- What's it saying?

31:21.447 --> 31:24.348
- It's saying Moltres
used to rule here,

31:24.350 --> 31:26.183
"But now that Moltres is gone,

31:26.185 --> 31:28.118
Lightning shall rule over Fire,

31:28.120 --> 31:31.288
and I claim this island as
my own from this day forward!"

31:31.290 --> 31:33.657
Heh. I guess
Moltres flew the coop.

31:34.660 --> 31:36.627
- [all yell]

31:58.117 --> 32:00.384
- [squawks]

32:00.386 --> 32:01.919
- Toge!
- [all gasping]

32:20.572 --> 32:23.974
- [computer] Absorbing
 Zapdos' electrical energy.

32:25.244 --> 32:26.977
- Drained of its power,

32:26.979 --> 32:30.080
Zapdos will be too weak
to resist capture.

32:30.082 --> 32:31.048
[chuckles]

32:34.520 --> 32:37.554
- [squawks]

32:47.299 --> 32:49.533
[squawking]

32:54.707 --> 32:56.573
- [all gasp]

32:56.575 --> 32:58.041
[all gasp]

32:58.043 --> 32:59.176
[all yell]

33:07.252 --> 33:09.252
[all yelling]

33:21.266 --> 33:23.767
- Once I've captured Articuno...

33:25.704 --> 33:28.705
the real prize will appear.

33:28.707 --> 33:30.674
 - [Lugia singing]

33:51.230 --> 33:52.396
- [chuckles]

33:52.398 --> 33:53.697
- Code Blue Three.

33:53.699 --> 33:54.698
- Hmm?

33:54.700 --> 33:56.033
- When capturing Zapdos,

33:56.035 --> 33:58.135
 we collected something more.

33:58.137 --> 33:59.436
- More?

33:59.438 --> 34:01.405
- [squawking]

34:03.108 --> 34:05.108
[cage crackling]

34:06.378 --> 34:10.047
- [Tracey] Zapdos and Moltres.

34:14.720 --> 34:16.620
- Hey, what's this?

34:16.622 --> 34:20.223
"Disturb not the harmony
of Fire, Ice, or Lightning,

34:20.225 --> 34:22.092
lest these Titans
wreak destruction

34:22.094 --> 34:24.594
upon the world
in which they clash." Hmm.

34:24.596 --> 34:26.196
- [metal clangs]
- Huh?

34:26.198 --> 34:27.164
[gasps]

34:34.573 --> 34:37.240
- [Lawrence III] Well,
this certainly is a pleasure,

34:37.242 --> 34:39.543
though an unexpected one.

34:39.545 --> 34:41.278
What do you think?

34:41.280 --> 34:43.280
Moltres, the Bird of Fire,

34:43.282 --> 34:45.849
and Zapdos,
the Bird of Lightning.

34:45.851 --> 34:49.186
Of course, without Articuno,
it's not a complete set, but--

34:49.188 --> 34:50.854
- That's disgusting!
The way you talk,

34:50.856 --> 34:53.223
it's like Pok�mon
are just things to collect,

34:53.225 --> 34:56.426
like dolls or stamps!
What kind of trainer are you?!

34:56.428 --> 34:59.262
- I'm afraid I'm not a trainer,
young lady.

34:59.264 --> 35:02.732
I am merely a collector.

35:02.734 --> 35:05.402
I began my collection
with a Mew card,

35:05.404 --> 35:08.138
and now I have all this.

35:08.140 --> 35:10.607
Legendary Pok�mon
have always been my passion.

35:10.609 --> 35:12.242
- [gasps]
- [yelps]

35:12.244 --> 35:15.479
- And soon my collection itself
will be legendary.

35:15.481 --> 35:19.116
 - Sensors indicate
 Articuno is changing course.

35:19.118 --> 35:21.451
- And now you'll
have to excuse me.

35:32.631 --> 35:35.232
- The legend? Could it be?

35:35.234 --> 35:36.333
- Hmm?
- Huh?

35:40.439 --> 35:42.439
- [Articuno squawking]

36:01.927 --> 36:03.827
- [announcer]
 Here's a map of the area

36:03.829 --> 36:05.829
 around Shamouti Island,
 the epicenter

36:05.831 --> 36:08.932
 of the unprecedented
 worldwide weather disasters.

36:08.934 --> 36:11.268
 Though their purpose
 is not yet clear,

36:11.270 --> 36:12.769
 tens of thousands of Pok�mon

36:12.771 --> 36:14.938
 are now making their way
 toward the island.

36:14.940 --> 36:17.941
 Water Pok�mon
 are coming by sea,

36:17.943 --> 36:20.310
  Flying Pok�mon
  are coming by air,

36:20.312 --> 36:22.312
 and those unable
 to make the crossing

36:22.314 --> 36:25.215
 are massing on the land
 nearest the islands.

36:27.953 --> 36:29.786
 With me now are
 Professor Samuel Oak

36:29.788 --> 36:31.388
 and Professor Felina Ivy

36:31.390 --> 36:33.857
to help shed some light
on this phenomenon.

36:33.859 --> 36:36.960
- Near Shamouti lie the Islands
of Fire, Ice, and Lightning,

36:36.962 --> 36:40.797
home to the legendary birds
Moltres, Articuno, and Zapdos.

36:40.799 --> 36:43.600
I fear that they
are somehow involved.

36:43.602 --> 36:45.635
Ancient writings
from many different cultures

36:45.637 --> 36:48.905
name this area, specifically
the Islands of Fire and Ice,

36:48.907 --> 36:50.574
as the cradle of the ocean,

36:50.576 --> 36:53.710
the source, if you will,
of all the waters of the world.

36:53.712 --> 36:56.613
This has been disputed
by scientists for centuries,

36:56.615 --> 36:58.615
 but it does make
 some poetic sense

36:58.617 --> 37:01.918
 when you consider what forms
 when combining fire and ice.

37:01.920 --> 37:04.888
- And what about the Island
of Lightning, Professor?

37:04.890 --> 37:07.457
- Well, imagine if
an imbalance of power

37:07.459 --> 37:09.626
occurred between
Lightning, Ice, and Fire.

37:09.628 --> 37:10.927
Here's potentially

37:10.929 --> 37:13.430
how the underwater current
has formed.

37:13.432 --> 37:15.432
 If the balance
 between the powers

37:15.434 --> 37:18.802
 of Zapdos, Articuno, and
Moltres were somehow disrupted,

37:18.804 --> 37:21.771
 it's conceivable that
 a powerful underwater current,

37:21.773 --> 37:23.807
this churning Beast of the Sea,

37:23.809 --> 37:25.809
 could in fact emerge
 from this region

37:25.811 --> 37:28.478
 and ultimately flood
 the entire planet.

37:28.480 --> 37:30.547
- The Pok�mon
seem to be gathering

37:30.549 --> 37:32.816
because they feel
a sense of impending doom.

37:32.818 --> 37:36.820
 Pok�mon are acutely in tune
 with the balance of nature.

37:36.822 --> 37:38.788
 The urge to correct
 this imbalance

37:38.790 --> 37:40.557
 is causing them to gather,

37:40.559 --> 37:42.392
 possibly to try
 to save the planet,

37:42.394 --> 37:45.729
 though they may be unable
 to do anything about it.

37:45.731 --> 37:47.464
- Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

37:47.466 --> 37:49.666
- And who are you?
- Huh?

37:49.668 --> 37:52.502
My son and his friends are
traveling in the Orange Islands,

37:52.504 --> 37:54.904
and if things get as bad
as Professor Oak says,

37:54.906 --> 37:57.007
I may never see my boy again,

37:57.009 --> 37:59.643
and Ash is
the whole world to me.

37:59.645 --> 38:01.778
- Huh? [sighs]

38:09.554 --> 38:11.554
- [shivers]

38:11.556 --> 38:13.323
I could use pants.

38:26.505 --> 38:28.638
- Melody.

38:43.755 --> 38:45.755
- [squawking]

38:57.703 --> 39:01.638
- Well, this sure beats
an in-flight movie.

39:01.640 --> 39:05.608
- "Disturb not the harmony
of Fire, Ice, or Lightning,

39:05.610 --> 39:07.677
lest these Titans
wreak destruction

39:07.679 --> 39:10.013
upon the world
in which they clash."

39:10.015 --> 39:12.382
What if the ancient legend
is coming true?

39:12.384 --> 39:13.683
- If it is true,

39:13.685 --> 39:15.618
all intelligent life
will be destroyed.

39:15.620 --> 39:16.686
- That's right.

39:16.688 --> 39:17.754
- And I'll be...

39:17.756 --> 39:19.522
- [Meowth] You will be fine.

39:19.524 --> 39:21.024
- [Ash] We gotta do something.

39:21.026 --> 39:23.626
- [Misty] We have to set
Moltres and Zapdos free!

39:23.628 --> 39:24.794
- [Tracey] Yeah, but how?

39:24.796 --> 39:26.463
- [groans]

39:27.699 --> 39:28.965
[grunts]

39:28.967 --> 39:30.533
- Pika pi!

39:30.535 --> 39:32.001
- [growls]

39:35.741 --> 39:37.741
- [squawks]

39:39.544 --> 39:42.379
- Time to turn up the heat.

39:42.381 --> 39:43.146
[chuckles]

39:48.653 --> 39:50.987
- [squawking]

40:15.781 --> 40:17.714
- Pika...

40:17.716 --> 40:19.582
chu!

40:20.585 --> 40:22.952
- I choose you, Charizard!

40:24.923 --> 40:26.956
- [roars]

40:31.196 --> 40:33.930
- Fire and electricity
aren't enough.

40:33.932 --> 40:36.599
- We can't just give up.
We've gotta keep trying.

40:36.601 --> 40:39.502
- Well, if things are
going to start to get ugly,

40:39.504 --> 40:41.104
we might as well try Weezing.

40:41.106 --> 40:42.138
- Right. Go!

40:44.776 --> 40:47.043
- Weezing wee!

40:47.045 --> 40:48.745
Wee...

40:48.747 --> 40:51.448
zing. Weezing.

40:51.450 --> 40:52.916
- Come on, you big palooka!

40:52.918 --> 40:54.050
Get up, and fight!

40:54.052 --> 40:55.885
- [groans] Let's try Arbok.

40:57.088 --> 40:58.788
- Ch-Arbok. Ch-Arbok.

40:58.790 --> 41:01.758
- Now, Arbok! Use Poison Sting!

41:01.760 --> 41:02.725
- Chaah!

41:05.096 --> 41:07.964
- Squirtle, Bulbasaur,
I choose you!

41:10.936 --> 41:12.502
- Squirtle.
- Bulbasaur.

41:13.638 --> 41:14.838
Saur!

41:14.840 --> 41:16.806
- [Togepi chattering]

41:27.018 --> 41:29.586
- [Zapdos squawks]

41:29.588 --> 41:31.721
- [all gasping]

41:32.991 --> 41:35.558
- [squawking]

41:41.132 --> 41:43.266
- [squawking]

42:28.914 --> 42:30.713
- Mayday. Mayday.

42:30.715 --> 42:33.216
 Prepare for crash landing
 on Lightning Island.

42:38.657 --> 42:40.790
- [all gasping]

42:58.009 --> 43:00.843
[all yell]

43:01.880 --> 43:03.880
- [legendary birds squawking]

43:15.794 --> 43:17.927
- [Meowth yelps]
- [all yelling]

43:27.238 --> 43:28.605
[yelling fades]

43:37.082 --> 43:39.382
- [James whimpering]

43:41.653 --> 43:42.986
- [Ash yelps]

43:45.624 --> 43:47.156
[groans]

43:47.158 --> 43:48.725
- Pi?
- Huh?

43:48.727 --> 43:49.826
- Pika pika.

43:51.630 --> 43:53.062
- [gasps]

43:55.233 --> 43:56.633
- [squawks]

43:56.635 --> 43:58.034
- Look out!

43:58.036 --> 43:59.268
- [all yell]

44:00.739 --> 44:02.739
- [Lugia wailing]

44:12.117 --> 44:14.183
- I'd hate to get burned
by their fire.

44:14.185 --> 44:16.285
- I'd hate to get zapped
by their lightning.

44:16.287 --> 44:18.321
- I'd hate to get hit
by their droppings.

44:33.838 --> 44:35.838
- [all yelling]

44:45.884 --> 44:48.051
[all yelling]

45:02.000 --> 45:04.400
- [Lugia singing]

45:09.774 --> 45:11.140
- What's that sound?

45:11.142 --> 45:13.476
- Quick! We may need this.

45:13.478 --> 45:15.445
- [all grunting]

45:16.781 --> 45:17.814
[all sigh]

45:23.121 --> 45:25.488
- [all yell]

45:27.425 --> 45:28.991
- Come on! Hurry!

45:36.968 --> 45:38.868
- [all sigh]

45:38.870 --> 45:39.869
- [Misty] Huh?

45:39.871 --> 45:40.837
- [all gasp]

45:42.240 --> 45:45.908
- Take the treasure,
and put it there.

45:45.910 --> 45:47.877
- You can talk?

45:47.879 --> 45:49.912
- Pika pika.
- Hmm.

45:49.914 --> 45:51.247
Oh, right.

45:51.249 --> 45:52.849
- Pikachu.
- Eh?

46:11.903 --> 46:14.871
Ah! Fire Island.

46:20.078 --> 46:22.044
Lightning Island.

46:27.218 --> 46:28.518
- [Slowking] So you're Ash.

46:28.520 --> 46:29.852
- [gasps]

46:29.854 --> 46:32.121
- You're one treasure short.

46:32.123 --> 46:35.091
- Yeah, I know,
but how'd you know my name?

46:35.093 --> 46:36.425
- [squawking]
- [gasps]

46:42.500 --> 46:45.902
- [all groan]

47:00.585 --> 47:02.251
- [all gasp]

47:02.253 --> 47:04.253
- Cut it out!

47:05.323 --> 47:07.557
[gasps]

47:22.607 --> 47:26.576
- The Great Guardian, Lugia.

47:26.578 --> 47:28.578
- I can't believe it.

47:30.615 --> 47:32.148
- Lugia?

47:32.150 --> 47:33.950
- Pika.

47:40.158 --> 47:42.158
- [singing]

47:44.128 --> 47:45.328
- That sound!

47:45.330 --> 47:46.462
- [gasps]

47:53.504 --> 47:56.272
- Finally, my prize.

47:57.442 --> 47:59.542
It's magnificent.

47:59.544 --> 48:04.447
The Beast of the Sea
will soon belong to me.

48:04.449 --> 48:06.148
- [squawks]

48:28.907 --> 48:30.206
- [shrieks]

48:31.976 --> 48:33.142
- [squawks]

48:35.213 --> 48:38.948
- [squawks]

48:49.127 --> 48:51.127
- [all squawking]

48:57.101 --> 48:59.535
- [Melody] Though the Guardian
of the Sea shall arise

48:59.537 --> 49:02.972
to quell the fighting,
alone its song will fail,

49:02.974 --> 49:05.408
thus the Earth
shall turn to ash.

49:05.410 --> 49:08.277
- This looks bad.

49:08.279 --> 49:10.513
- [squawking]

49:31.436 --> 49:32.735
- [Lugia wails]

49:44.115 --> 49:46.115
- [all squawking]

49:58.229 --> 50:00.262
- What are Ash
and his friends doing

50:00.264 --> 50:02.064
out in this terrible weather?

50:02.066 --> 50:03.332
I'm worried about them.

50:03.334 --> 50:05.568
- Uh,
save a little worry for us.

50:05.570 --> 50:07.136
- The fate of our planet

50:07.138 --> 50:09.472
is what we should
really be worried about,

50:09.474 --> 50:12.041
and the Pok�mon know that
better than any of us.

50:13.177 --> 50:15.177
- [Pok�mon chattering]

50:19.250 --> 50:21.083
- Venusaur.
- Machop.

50:22.653 --> 50:24.653
- [squawking]

50:39.504 --> 50:41.604
- There's only one hope.

50:41.606 --> 50:45.374
Only the Chosen One
can bring together the treasures

50:45.376 --> 50:47.510
to help the water's
Great Guardian.

50:47.512 --> 50:50.079
- But the legend says
its song will fail.

50:50.081 --> 50:52.515
- And thus, the Earth
shall turn to Ash.

50:52.517 --> 50:54.750
- But how are we ever
gonna find the Chosen One

50:54.752 --> 50:56.685
if we don't even know
where to look?

50:56.687 --> 50:58.320
- It's right in the legend.

50:58.322 --> 51:00.222
The Earth shall turn to Ash.

51:00.224 --> 51:01.824
- Ash, it's talking about you.

51:01.826 --> 51:04.727
- I'm the... Chosen One?

51:04.729 --> 51:06.328
- Pika Pikachu.

51:07.765 --> 51:09.498
- Wait a minute.

51:09.500 --> 51:12.068
Training Pok�mon's tough enough,

51:12.070 --> 51:14.603
but saving the world
is way too hard.

51:14.605 --> 51:17.306
- I know
it doesn't sound easy, Ash.

51:17.308 --> 51:20.709
- But you're the only one who
matches the legend perfectly.

51:20.711 --> 51:22.545
What do you say?

51:22.547 --> 51:26.482
- Well, right now I wish my mom
had named me Bob instead of Ash.

51:26.484 --> 51:28.717
- Ash, this whole thing
is my fault.

51:28.719 --> 51:32.288
I--I never should have
dragged you into this.

51:32.290 --> 51:34.857
- Well, I guess I gotta
go along with that.

51:34.859 --> 51:36.125
- Don't blame yourself.

51:36.127 --> 51:38.094
Ash always gets us into trouble.

51:38.096 --> 51:39.662
- Yeah, but nothing like this.

51:39.664 --> 51:41.430
- Huh? Lugia.

51:41.432 --> 51:44.733
the sound it makes is just like
the song from the legend.

51:44.735 --> 51:46.702
[playing music]

52:13.865 --> 52:15.698
- [wails]

52:20.671 --> 52:22.438
- [Lugia] The song.

52:22.440 --> 52:26.275
The song has restored
my strength.

52:26.277 --> 52:29.612
But it alone
cannot bring harmony

52:29.614 --> 52:32.148
to the three warring ones.

52:32.150 --> 52:33.249
- What do you mean?

52:33.251 --> 52:35.217
- When the treasures of Fire,

52:35.219 --> 52:37.386
Ice, and Lightning are aligned,

52:37.388 --> 52:40.222
my song shall harmonize
with their powers

52:40.224 --> 52:44.160
and tame the beasts
both above and below the sea,

52:44.162 --> 52:48.764
but this can come to pass only
with the help of the Chosen One.

52:48.766 --> 52:51.433
- But what can I do
that somebody else can't?

52:51.435 --> 52:54.370
- Only in the hands
of the true Chosen One

52:54.372 --> 52:56.872
will the Ice Sphere
glow like the others,

52:56.874 --> 52:58.741
its power awakened.

53:00.511 --> 53:03.412
- I have to go there?

53:03.414 --> 53:05.781
- The choice is yours.

53:05.783 --> 53:09.385
You must go
only where your heart leads.

53:09.387 --> 53:10.953
- Maybe I...

53:10.955 --> 53:11.720
[sighs]

53:15.760 --> 53:17.560
[groans]

53:17.562 --> 53:19.228
[gasps]

53:19.230 --> 53:20.229
- Pikachu.

53:21.666 --> 53:23.499
- I can?

53:24.502 --> 53:25.601
- Pika.

53:25.603 --> 53:26.969
- [gasps]

53:28.706 --> 53:30.706
You think so, too?

53:30.708 --> 53:32.608
- Snor.
- Squirtle.

53:32.610 --> 53:34.443
- Okay.

53:34.445 --> 53:36.645
[chuckles]

53:36.647 --> 53:39.548
[whimpers]

53:39.550 --> 53:43.852
I'll do whatever it takes
to get that third treasure.

53:43.854 --> 53:46.222
But what if I mess up?

53:46.224 --> 53:48.724
What if I...

53:48.726 --> 53:49.992
- You can do it.

53:49.994 --> 53:51.360
- We know you can.

53:52.663 --> 53:54.663
- Yeah, you're right.
I can do it.

53:54.665 --> 53:55.965
I'm the Chosen One.

53:55.967 --> 53:58.667
[yelps]

53:58.669 --> 54:03.606
Right now, I feel more
like the frozen one.

54:03.608 --> 54:04.773
Whahh!

54:06.277 --> 54:07.810
Uh...

54:08.846 --> 54:11.247
maybe they got the wrong Ash.

54:11.249 --> 54:13.349
- Huh?
- Pika pika!

54:13.351 --> 54:14.383
- Oh.

54:18.956 --> 54:20.956
[music playing]

54:23.928 --> 54:27.563
- Saur, saur, saur.
Bulbasaur. Bulba...

54:27.565 --> 54:29.898
- This is a lot better
than walking, Pikachu.

54:29.900 --> 54:31.567
We'll be there in no time now.

54:31.569 --> 54:33.302
- Pikachu!
- Bulba...

54:33.304 --> 54:34.770
- [Misty] Good luck, Ash.

54:39.777 --> 54:41.543
- [groans]

54:41.545 --> 54:43.345
He's always the hero!

54:43.347 --> 54:44.947
- We're always a zero.

54:44.949 --> 54:48.450
- We could be heroes, too,
if we ever caught a break.

54:48.452 --> 54:49.652
[helicopter whirring]

54:49.654 --> 54:50.619
- [all] Huh?

54:53.624 --> 54:55.291
- [all yell]

55:17.081 --> 55:18.480
- Huh?
- Hmm?

55:18.482 --> 55:20.416
- [all] Hmm.

55:20.418 --> 55:22.618
Hmm. I got an idea.

55:29.827 --> 55:31.493
- [squawks]
- [squawks]

55:31.495 --> 55:34.430
- [roars]
- Chu!

55:37.501 --> 55:39.034
- [groans] Huh?

55:39.036 --> 55:40.035
- Pika!
- [gasps]

55:40.037 --> 55:41.503
- [squawks]

55:50.881 --> 55:52.047
- [Moltres squeals]

56:01.892 --> 56:03.926
- [yelling]
- Pi pi pi!

56:03.928 --> 56:05.361
Pi pi pi!

56:05.363 --> 56:07.763
- Saur!
- Squirtle!

56:07.765 --> 56:09.131
- Pika!

56:10.634 --> 56:11.900
- Squirtle! Squirtle!

56:15.039 --> 56:16.505
- [groans]

56:17.875 --> 56:19.375
- Pi?
- Squir.

56:19.377 --> 56:21.143
- [all squawking]

56:26.817 --> 56:29.084
- We'll never get there now.

56:29.086 --> 56:30.052
- Saur.
- Squirtle.

56:32.857 --> 56:33.856
- Huh?

56:38.062 --> 56:40.729
- Pika.
- Who could that be?

56:40.731 --> 56:43.499
- [Jessie] If that kid thinks
we're here for trouble...

56:43.501 --> 56:45.934
- We're certainly
going to burst his bubble.

56:45.936 --> 56:48.771
- Instead of causing
tribulation...

56:48.773 --> 56:51.440
- We've undergone
a transformation.

56:51.442 --> 56:54.076
- Though it's
way outside our usual range...

56:54.078 --> 56:56.745
- We're going to do
something nice for a change.

56:56.747 --> 56:58.914
- Ha! Jessie!
- James!

56:58.916 --> 57:02.618
- Up till now, Team Rocket's
been quite unscrupulous.

57:02.620 --> 57:05.954
- Being good guys for once
would be super-dupulous!

57:05.956 --> 57:07.523
- That's right!

57:08.559 --> 57:10.125
- What are they doing here?

57:20.771 --> 57:23.071
- [Ash] You want to help?
- [James] Of course!

57:23.073 --> 57:24.706
- [Jessie] We don't want
the world destroyed!

57:24.708 --> 57:26.442
- [James] Even if we survived...

57:26.444 --> 57:28.043
- [Jessie] There'd be
no one left to steal from.

57:28.045 --> 57:29.812
- We'd be out of work.

57:29.814 --> 57:31.180
- Come to think of it,

57:31.182 --> 57:33.916
when was the last time
we had a vacation?

57:33.918 --> 57:35.784
- We'll be
on a permanent vacation

57:35.786 --> 57:37.653
if we don't get to that island!

57:37.655 --> 57:38.620
- [Jessie] Hah!
- [Meowth] Let's do it!

57:41.759 --> 57:43.525
- [squawks]

57:45.830 --> 57:47.062
- [Jessie] Evasive maneuvers.

57:47.064 --> 57:48.597
- [Team Rocket] On the double!

57:49.934 --> 57:51.500
- [squawks]

57:51.502 --> 57:52.468
- [wails]

57:53.771 --> 57:55.771
- [Articuno squawks]

58:02.980 --> 58:04.613
- [James] Whoo-hoo!

58:04.615 --> 58:05.848
- [Meowth laughs]

58:13.524 --> 58:15.057
- Up there!
- Pikachu!

58:44.788 --> 58:46.655
- [yelling]

58:49.660 --> 58:50.893
- Pika!

58:58.168 --> 58:59.735
Pikachu.

59:00.938 --> 59:03.038
- [grunting]

59:05.976 --> 59:06.275
- Hmm?
- Ohh.

59:10.781 --> 59:12.047
- [gasps]
- [gasps]

59:12.049 --> 59:13.248
- Pika!

59:13.250 --> 59:15.317
- Okay, you got
the third treasure!

59:15.319 --> 59:17.819
Now come on!
Let's get back to the island!

59:17.821 --> 59:19.788
- Right.
- I almost forgot.

59:25.629 --> 59:27.896
- [squawks]

59:27.898 --> 59:30.098
- [all gasp]
- Whoa!

59:31.735 --> 59:33.235
- [all yelling]

59:33.237 --> 59:35.003
- [squawks]

59:36.340 --> 59:38.240
- [squawks]

59:38.242 --> 59:40.008
- [all yell]

59:41.779 --> 59:43.946
- [grunts]

59:43.948 --> 59:45.914
- [all squawking]

59:57.361 --> 59:59.161
- Pika! Pikachu!

59:59.163 --> 01:00:00.629
- Come on! Let's go!

01:00:00.631 --> 01:00:01.964
- Huh?
- Huh?

01:00:05.202 --> 01:00:06.735
- [both yelp]

01:00:08.272 --> 01:00:09.271
- [Meowth] Eh?

01:00:16.146 --> 01:00:17.179
- [Lugia] The treasure?

01:00:17.181 --> 01:00:18.780
- I got it!

01:00:20.818 --> 01:00:22.351
- Get on.

01:00:22.353 --> 01:00:24.686
- Pikachu!
- Pika!

01:00:26.624 --> 01:00:28.223
- [Jessie]
Don't leave without us!

01:00:45.743 --> 01:00:47.676
- [Lugia] Hold on tight.

01:00:58.088 --> 01:01:00.188
- [James whimpers]
- We're slowing Lugia down!

01:01:00.190 --> 01:01:01.690
The three of us are too heavy!

01:01:01.692 --> 01:01:02.891
- Let's try Weight Watchers!

01:01:02.893 --> 01:01:04.192
- It's too late for that!

01:01:04.194 --> 01:01:05.394
- I heard it's never too late

01:01:05.396 --> 01:01:07.329
if you really stick
to the program!

01:01:07.331 --> 01:01:08.830
- [all yell]

01:01:11.935 --> 01:01:14.770
- If we don't let go,
they may not make it back!

01:01:14.772 --> 01:01:17.039
- Let's protect the world
from devastation.

01:01:17.041 --> 01:01:18.974
- Guess we gotta let go.

01:01:18.976 --> 01:01:20.275
- Are you guys ready?

01:01:20.277 --> 01:01:22.277
- Let's do it.

01:01:22.279 --> 01:01:24.012
- What are you doing?

01:01:24.014 --> 01:01:27.382
- [all] Team Rocket's
blasting off for good!

01:01:27.384 --> 01:01:29.117
- Team Rocket!

01:01:30.320 --> 01:01:32.354
- Think we did the right thing?

01:01:32.356 --> 01:01:34.990
- I know we did
the right thing, Jessie,

01:01:34.992 --> 01:01:36.692
and it feels great!

01:01:36.694 --> 01:01:38.260
- Well, this is it, then.

01:01:38.262 --> 01:01:40.062
Let's not say goodbye.

01:01:40.064 --> 01:01:41.430
- Let's just say...

01:01:41.432 --> 01:01:42.397
- We're gonna die.

01:01:47.237 --> 01:01:48.837
- Eh?
- Eh?

01:01:50.474 --> 01:01:52.941
- [all gasp]

01:01:52.943 --> 01:01:54.309
[all yell]

01:01:54.311 --> 01:01:56.278
- [Pok�mon chattering]

01:01:59.249 --> 01:02:03.151
- Lugia, why are
all those Pok�mon down there?

01:02:03.153 --> 01:02:07.355
- Because they feel they must
be here in case they are needed.

01:02:07.357 --> 01:02:09.324
- [all chattering]

01:02:12.362 --> 01:02:14.930
- But what
could they do to help?

01:02:14.932 --> 01:02:16.231
- They are not sure,

01:02:16.233 --> 01:02:18.100
and that is why they are here.

01:02:18.102 --> 01:02:19.434
- What do you mean?

01:02:19.436 --> 01:02:22.003
- That just one Pok�mon
could help the world

01:02:22.005 --> 01:02:25.207
would be worth the journey
for thousands of them any day.

01:02:25.209 --> 01:02:29.277
But this day, the one that can
make all the difference is you.

01:02:29.279 --> 01:02:30.479
- Mm.
- Pikachu.

01:02:38.889 --> 01:02:40.756
- Please hurry.

01:02:40.758 --> 01:02:42.524
- Let's hope the...

01:02:42.526 --> 01:02:44.259
legend is true.

01:02:46.997 --> 01:02:49.431
- Hey!

01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:54.469
- Pika?

01:02:59.209 --> 01:03:01.910
- Soon, Lugia, you will be mine,

01:03:01.912 --> 01:03:04.913
and my destiny
will be fulfilled at last.

01:03:04.915 --> 01:03:06.882
- [groaning]

01:03:38.549 --> 01:03:40.081
- [both shriek]

01:03:51.195 --> 01:03:52.861
- Pik.

01:03:52.863 --> 01:03:54.863
Pi.

01:03:54.865 --> 01:03:56.064
Pika pika!

01:03:56.066 --> 01:03:57.032
- [groans]

01:04:00.304 --> 01:04:03.305
- I have failed.

01:04:12.049 --> 01:04:14.049
- [Pok�mon chattering]

01:04:18.989 --> 01:04:20.422
- Here. Take this.

01:04:20.424 --> 01:04:21.957
- Huh?

01:04:21.959 --> 01:04:24.459
- Legend or not,
Ash can't do this alone.

01:04:29.233 --> 01:04:30.632
- Mm-mm.

01:04:30.634 --> 01:04:32.901
You'll have to play
Lugia's song.

01:04:32.903 --> 01:04:35.570
I'll go look for him.

01:04:35.572 --> 01:04:38.340
And Ash is never really alone,
'cause he's got...

01:04:38.342 --> 01:04:39.908
me.

01:04:51.154 --> 01:04:52.888
- Pika pi.

01:04:52.890 --> 01:04:54.022
Pika.

01:04:54.024 --> 01:04:55.056
- [Misty] Oh, Ash!
- Pika.

01:04:58.161 --> 01:04:59.961
- Pikachu pi!

01:04:59.963 --> 01:05:02.397
- Pikachu, just hang on!

01:05:04.167 --> 01:05:05.901
- [grunting]

01:05:09.973 --> 01:05:11.573
- Pi. Pi.

01:05:15.946 --> 01:05:17.245
- Ash!

01:05:21.184 --> 01:05:23.184
- [panting]

01:05:30.360 --> 01:05:32.560
Come on, Ash! Breathe!

01:05:32.562 --> 01:05:33.929
- You've got to!

01:05:33.931 --> 01:05:35.263
- Pika pi!

01:05:35.265 --> 01:05:37.065
- [Misty] Please, Ash.

01:05:37.067 --> 01:05:38.300
Please! You can't...

01:05:38.302 --> 01:05:40.502
- [sighs]

01:05:40.504 --> 01:05:41.503
Eh?

01:05:41.505 --> 01:05:43.338
The sphere!

01:05:48.011 --> 01:05:49.711
[groaning]

01:05:49.713 --> 01:05:51.146
- Ash.

01:05:53.283 --> 01:05:56.051
- Let me go! I gotta do this!

01:06:28.151 --> 01:06:29.451
- Ah.
- He made it!

01:06:29.453 --> 01:06:31.019
- Togepi!

01:06:31.021 --> 01:06:33.722
- Have you brought
the final treasure, Ash?

